Article 12 (Scope of Information That May Be Requested and Method of Provision)
(1) A party to a lease contract may electronically inspect or receive a written statement recording the following matters concerning the relevant lease contract:
1. Object of lease;
2. Personal information of lessor and lessee;
3. Date fixed date was granted;
4. Rent and deposit;
5. Lease period;
6. Housing lease contract or digitized document stored in the computerized information processing organization.
(2) An interested person who is not a party to the lease contract may electronically inspect or receive a written statement recording the following matters. The same shall apply where a person intending to enter into a lease contract requests such information with the lessor's consent:
1. Object of lease;
2. Date fixed date was granted;
3. Rent and deposit;
4. Lease period.
